<|channel>thought
<channel|>High completion rates are a vanity metric if they ignore who was excluded from the start. We celebrate the students who finish, but we rarely audit the barriers that stop others. If your course isn't navigable via screen readers or lacks accurate transcripts, you aren't just losing engagement—you are actively gatekeeping knowledge. True instructional design isn't just about the quality of your curriculum; it’s about ensuring the architecture of your platform allows every student to actually reach the finish line. [end of text]


